        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "012db5b1-1929-56a0-94f6-90e1bf38000b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Yorkshire Terrier, Cavalier King Charles Spaniel, Chihuahua, Papillon, Pointer\n- People: Ronald Reagan, Nancy Reagan\n- Medical conditions: Hypoplasia of dens\n- Places: Yorkshire, England\n- Roles: President of the United States\n- Animals: Rex\n\nFacts:\n- The Yorkshire Terrier was developed during the 19th century in Yorkshire, England, to catch rats in clothing mills.\n- The Yorkshire Terrier is a small dog breed of terrier type.\n- The Cavalier King Charles Spaniel is a small spaniel that The Kennel Club and the American Kennel Club classify as a toy dog.\n- Hypoplasia of dens is more commonly seen in the Chihuahua, the Papillon, the Pointer, and the Yorkshire Terrier.\n- Rex was born on December 16, 1984, and died on August 31, 1998.\n- Rex was a Cavalier King Charles Spaniel owned by Ronald Reagan and Nancy Reagan during Ronald Reagan's term as President of the United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
